  "body": "**Stacked on #1123** (issue #532, the Wire Contour op; itself on #560, #551). Until those merge, this PR's diff also shows their commits. The commit for this issue is the last one on the branch. Retarget or merge after #1123.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0 (process files at PROCESS_VERSION 17).\n\n## What changed\n\nA Wire Contour mounts no library tool (#532), so its `Operation::tool` is the empty word. Each reader changed below checks `KindInfo::mounts_tool()` and nothing else: no kind matches, no \"is the name empty\" checks. A milling op whose tool was deleted still mounts a tool, so it is refused or listed exactly as before. Each surface has a pinning test for that too.\n\n| Surface | Before | Now |\n|---|---|---|\n| Program stock sim (`stock_sim.rs` plan walk, new `stock_sim_wire.rs`) | `Die1: tool  is not in the library` | `plan_program` leaves the wire cut out of the plan, the same way the probe and torch arms do. `simulate_document` refuses by name: `Die1: a wire cut is verified by the wire laws, not the stock sim`. The post gate shows this as its non-blocking \"not judged\" line, and the setup sheet's sim line says \"SIM: not judged - ...\". |\n| Setup sheet, op row (`setup_sheet/operations.rs`) | empty TOOL cell | TOOL cell `cond C110`, and under the row `CONDITION C110  WIRE D 0.250  GAP 0.040`, read through `wire_op::condition_of` (the door generation uses). A condition the machine no longer states prints `! wire condition: <refusal>`. |\n| Setup sheet, tool table (`setup_sheet/tools.rs`) | `(tool '' is no longer in the document)` | No change in this file: it reads `tool_list::for_setup`, which no longer has the row. A wire setup prints \"(no tools in this setup)\". |\n| Tool list / export (`tool_list.rs`, `tool_list_export.rs`) | a row for tool `\"\"` | No row. A wire EDM has no tool table. The export reads the same rows, so no change was needed in it. |\n| Cutting data (`cutting.rs`, found in the audit) | `tool  is not in the library` | `a Wire Contour mounts no library tool - its cut is the machine's EDM condition, and the cutting-data table speaks for milling tools only` |\n\n`stock_sim.rs` gets only three touches, to keep the later merge with #1140 a keep-both: the `#[path]` module line, a 3-line skip arm, and one call line. The file was already 421 lines before this PR (now 428). The new logic is in `stock_sim_wire.rs` rather than added to it.\n\nWhy refuse the verdict instead of only skipping the cut: judging the uncut stock would report rest material wherever the wire cut through, which is a wrong answer. A program that mixes a wire EDM setup with a mill setup is already refused by the carry law (two machines), so no gouge verdict is lost today. Decisions: `docs/decisions/1110-wire-tool-readers.md`.\n\n## Audit of the other `op.tool` readers\n\n| File | Verdict on a wire cut | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cutting.rs` | **fixed** (above) | `suggest` looked the empty name up as a library tool. |\n| `fixture_struck.rs` (`op_hits`) | fine | No tool means `Ok(vec![])` (no hits). This file is display only (it tints the struck fixture) and feeds no post. A wire cut's workholding verdicts belong to the wire laws (#534). A milling op with a lost tool is still refused at the post by `tool_gate::tool_problem_of`. |\n| `fixture_carried.rs` (`carried_fixture_problems`) | fine | No tool means `tool_r = 0.0`, which is only the carry lattice's sizing radius. The fixture-in-carried-body check still runs on the carried body. |\n| `operation/footprint.rs` | fine | Only the `Face` arm reads the tool. A Wire Contour takes the `_ => Some(region)` arm, so its footprint is its profile region. |\n| `posting_index_swing.rs` | fine | A wire EDM states no work A axis, so `work_a` is `None` and the loop `continue`s before the tool is read. The post refuses a wire cut by name first anyway (`op_streams`, #532). |\n| `tool_numbers.rs` (`clash`, `clash_per_machine`) | fine | `\"\"` is not in `numbers()`, so it is skipped (\"not a tool: the post names that refusal itself\"). An empty name can never clash with a real tool. |\n| `sim_tool_body.rs`, `rest/ahead.rs` (outside the issue's list, read while auditing) | fine | No tool means `Ok(None)` (nothing to spin) and no rest mask, the same as a never-cutting op. |\n\n## Tests\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/wire_readers.rs`. Its gate map covers app::stock_sim, app::setup_sheet, app::tool_list, app::tool_list_export, app::cutting and app::posting_sim. It has 7 tests, and each surface gets one wire pin and one milling-missing-tool pin:\n\n- `the_program_sim_answers_a_wire_cut_by_name` (also covers `verification_report().not_judged` and `setup_sheet::simulate_verdict`)\n- `a_milling_op_with_a_missing_tool_is_still_refused_by_the_program_sim`\n- `the_setup_sheet_shows_the_wire_condition_and_no_missing_tool`\n- `the_setup_sheet_still_says_a_milling_tool_is_gone`\n- `the_tool_list_and_its_export_hold_no_row_for_a_wire_cut`\n- `the_tool_list_keeps_a_row_for_a_lost_milling_tool`\n- `the_cutting_data_table_says_why_it_cannot_speak_for_a_wire_cut` (also checks that the milling refusal text is unchanged)\n\nGate: the full `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head `d3c517cc` was green in 17.3 min, with 0 failed across post, motion, app and ui (2918 passed, 24 ignored). The stack's diff pulls in the shared CL goldens, so nearly every app suite ran, setup_sheet, tool_list, stock_sim_document, sim, cutting_data, wire_contour, edm_conditions, edm_machine, golden_cl and wire_readers among them. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` was clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The UI: the feeds page would now show the cutting-data refusal text for a wire cut. Whether a wire op shows that page at all is #535's.\n- The stock view and the MCP render overlay on a wire document. They walk `plan_program`, which now skips the cut, but no test drives them on a wire document.\n- A program mixing wire and mill setups: the carry law refuses it before this code is reached.\n- No snapshot PNGs, post scripts, verification laws, op/machine pages or contour-generator changes.\n\nChangelog: The program stock sim, setup sheet, tool list and cutting data handle a Wire Contour (no library tool): the sim refuses by name, the sheet shows the EDM condition, wire diameter and gap, and the tool list has no empty row (#1110)\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #1110\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
